  "projects": {
    "2016": [
      {
        "title": "Precise Garbage Collection for D",
        "short_description": "Implementing precise collection as a first step towards a better garbage collector.",
        "description": "<p>Implementing precise collection as a first step towards a better garbage collector.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "JDeHaan",
        "code_url": "https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-UTFTbYro4vQzJnR1NQa3E4WTA",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/5710606233501696/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Improvements for dstep.",
        "short_description": "This is a project to improve the dstep conversion tool. The major goal is to extend dstep to the point in which it is able to create bindings for the...",
        "description": "<p>This is a project to improve the dstep conversion tool. The major goal is to extend dstep to the point in which it is able to create bindings for the most of existing C libraries (in particular libclang bindings that are used by the dstep itself).</p>\n",
        "student_name": "ciechowoj",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/ciechowoj/dstep/commits/master?author=ciechowoj",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/5732312192909312/"
      },
      {
        "title": "A replacement of std.xml for the Phobos standard library",
        "short_description": "XML is probably the most used storage and interchange format for structured and semi-structured data, being also used for object serialization and...",
        "description": "<p>XML is probably the most used storage and interchange format for structured and semi-structured data, being also used for object serialization and configuration files.\nA good XML library is fundamental for many large applications; as such, shipping with a well-written std.xml would greatly benefit Phobos and more generally the D ecosystem.\nThe goal of this project is to produce a library for handling the XML format and replace the current std.xml with it.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Lodovico Giaretta",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/lodo1995/experimental.xml/tree/v0.1.2",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/5056473587515392/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Science for D - a non-uniform RNG",
        "short_description": "D is a modern language that offers the convenience of Python at the speed of C++. While D is constantly evolving, its support for scientific research...",
        "description": "<p>D is a modern language that offers the convenience of Python at the speed of C++. While D is constantly evolving, its support for scientific research is still sparse. This project will be focused on improving Mir (Phobos’s upcoming science module) by adding a universal non-uniform random number generator (RNG) based on Tinflex. In contrast to the standard acceptance-rejection method, Tinflex requires only knowledge of the probability density function, its first two derivatives and a partitioning in intervals with at most one inflection point and is thus easier to use. Moreover a lot of common non-uniform random distributions will be added.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Greenify",
        "code_url": "http://forum.dlang.org/post/ckwjysezxagpnrdkbtpq@forum.dlang.org",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/4617597723082752/"
      }
    ],
    "2019": [
      {
        "title": "Reference-Counted Data Structures for D",
        "short_description": "Currently, D’s built-in data structures (arrays and associative arrays) and\nPhobos collections (e.g. std.container.rbtree) rely on garbage...",
        "description": "<p>Currently, D’s built-in data structures (arrays and associative arrays) and\nPhobos collections (e.g. <code>std.container.rbtree</code>) rely on garbage collection.\nThis has a number of issues, including the inability to use them when compiling\nwith <code>-betterC</code>, GC pauses, and memory usage being nondeterministic.</p>\n<p>The goal of this project is to implement <code>@nogc @safe</code> versions of common data\nstructures through the use of reference counting for memory management.\nReference counting is already being used with success by other systems\nprogramming languages (such as C++) for the same purpose. With recent work by\nEduard Staniloiu on <a href=\"https://github.com/dlang/druntime/pull/2608\" target=\"_blank\"><code>__RefCount</code></a>,  an official implementation of these\ncollections can be added to D’s standard runtime.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "lesderid",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/dlang/druntime/pull/2760",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/6372712585363456/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Dataframes for D",
        "short_description": "This project aims at bringing native dataframes to D Programming Language. The main task would be to implement a dataframe which supports...",
        "description": "<p>This project aims at bringing native dataframes to D Programming Language. The main task would be to implement a dataframe which supports multi-indexing, column binary operations, grouping and data aggregation. Along with the dataframe will also come functionality to parse data from and write data to a CSV file without any hassle.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Prateek Nayak",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/Kriyszig/08316365281c050c8994a1783307ec19",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/6700435165937664/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Header generation for C/C++",
        "short_description": "Automated C/C++ header generation from D files",
        "description": "<p>Automated C/C++ header generation from D files</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Eduard Staniloiu",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/edi33416/d2f8afff217e64deae368e0e81f2adcf",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/5282070350266368/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Replace Runtime Hooks with Templates",
        "short_description": "D’s betterC mode is an important tool to be able to use D on bare-metal and embedded platforms. By disabling, for example the class support, the...",
        "description": "<p>D’s betterC mode is an important tool to be able to use D on bare-metal and embedded platforms. By disabling, for example the class support, the compiles does not need to as many runtime functions and types to be implemented for the code to compile and link. This makes the life of a bare-metal developer much easier.</p>\n<p>But there is a catch! A lot of the language features runtime hooks, which in turn requires the TypeInfo class to be able to function. One way of solving both of these problems is by moving runtime hooks to use templates instead. This solves the betterC by removing the dependency of classes (the TypeInfo class), and it solves the safety issue because now the compiler will have all the information about the hook and it can verify it itself and not just trust that the runtime developer remembered to mark the hook correctly.</p>\n<p>This proposal will work on translating all the array hooks from using the TypeInfo class to templates.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Dan Printzell",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/Vild/GSOC2019/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/5343585740783616/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Independency of D from the C Standard Library",
        "short_description": "An effort to decouple D from the C standard library.",
        "description": "<p>An effort to decouple D from the C standard library.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Stefanos Baziotis",
        "code_url": "http://users.uoa.gr/~sdi1600105/google-summer-of-code.html",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/4735613390028800/"
      }
    ],
    "2025": []
  },
